            <title>0.17.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:54:56 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1700</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.17.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.17.0</h2>
<p><b>Jarvis stays with you all day now.</b> Closing the window no longer quits
the app — Jarvis moves to the menu bar, keeps watching your sources, and greets
you once each morning with what the day holds.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Jarvis lives in the menu bar.</b> The red button hides the window
      instead of quitting. Your day, your route and an unsent note survive it.
      Click the menu-bar owl to bring it back; the menu's first line says what
      needs you and when your sources last synced. Quit with ⌘Q.</li>
  <li><b>A morning greeting.</b> Once a day, when you wake your Mac, a small
      panel says good morning and counts your meetings. Click it to open your
      day, or ignore it and it leaves on its own. Switch it off in
      Settings → Focus, where you can also start Jarvis at login.</li>
  <li><b>Updates install themselves.</b> From this version on, a new release
      downloads quietly in the background and installs the next time you quit
      Jarvis. No more update dialogs to click through.</li>
  <li><b>A sign-in window that opens at a readable size</b>, with the owl awake
      while it waits for you.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
